{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"string","title":"String (Immutable)","group":"","order":10,"html":"<p>1. Sequence of characters</p>\n<p>2. Used to store text data like data read from a file</p>\n<p>3. Typically small set of characters</p>\n<p>4. character 'A' to 'Z' are stored as values from 65 to 90</p>\n<p>5. character 'a' to 'z' are stored as values from 97 to 122</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>print(ord('a'))\n\nprint(ord('A'))\n\nprint(ord('z'))\n\nprint(ord('Z'))\n\nprint(ord('0'))\n\nprint(ord('9'))\n\nprint(ord(' '))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>print(chr(97))\n\nprint(chr(65))\n\nprint(chr(122))\n\nprint(chr(90))\n\nprint(chr(48))\n\nprint(chr(57))\n\nprint(chr(32))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = 'geek'\n\nprint(s)\n\nprint(type(s))\n\nprint(s[0])\n\nprint(s[1])\n\nprint(s[2])\n\nprint(s[3])\n\nprint(s[-1])\n\nprint(s[-2])\n\nprint(s[-3])\n\nprint(s[-4])</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = ''' welcome to my world'''\n\nprint(s)\n\nprint(type(s))</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Escape sequences</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = 'Welcome to my world'\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = 'Welcome to my worl'd'\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = 'Welcome to my worl\\'d'\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = \"Hi, \\nI'm fine\"\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s1 = 'A simple \\example'\n\nprint(s1)\n\ns2 = 'A simple example \\\\'\n\nprint(s2)\n\ns3 = 'A simple \\t example '\n\nprint(s3)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Raw Strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s1 = 'c:\\project\\name.py'\n\nprint(s1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s1 = r'c:\\project\\name.py'\n\nprint(s1)\n\ns1 = R'c:\\project\\name.py'\n\nprint(s1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Formatted Strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># using '%'\n\nname = 'ABC'\ncourse = 'Python Course'\n\ns = 'Welcome %s to %s' %(name, course)\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># using format()\n\nname = 'ABC'\ncourse = 'Python Course'\n\ns = 'Welcome {} to {}'.format(name, course)\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># using f-string\n\nname = 'ABC'\ncourse = 'Python Course'\n\ns = f'Welcome {name} to {course}'\n\nprint(s)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Example\n\na = 10\nb = 20\n\nprint(f'Sum of {a} and {b} is {a+b}')</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Example\n\na = 'ABC'\nb = 'abc'\nprint(f\"lower case of {a} is {b.lower()}\")\nprint(f\"upper case of {b} is {a.upper()}\")</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>String comparison</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s1 = 'gfg'\ns2 = 'ide'\n\nprint(s1 == s2)\n\nprint(s1 != s2)\n\nprint(s1 &gt; s2)\n\nprint(s1 &lt; s2)\n\nprint(s1 &gt;= s2)\n\nprint(s1 &lt;= s2)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>String Operations</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Check for Substrings\n\n'''\nsubstrings of 'ABCD' are 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'AB', 'BC', 'CD', 'ABCD'\n'''\n\ns1 = 'geeksforgeeks'\ns2 = 'geeks'\n\nprint(s2 in s1) # True\n\nprint(s2 not in s1) # False\n\nprint(s1 in s2) # False\n\nprint(s1 not in s2) # True</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Concatenation\n\ns1 = 'geeks'\ns2 = 'for'\ns3 = 'geeks'\n\nprint(s1 + s2 + s3)\n\nprint(s1 + ' ' + s2 + ' ' + s3)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Finding position of a substring\n\ns1 = 'geeksforgeeks'\ns2 = 'geeks'\n\nprint(s1.index(s2))  # First come\n\nprint(s1.rindex(s2))  # Last come\n\nprint(s1.index(s2, 0, 13)) # Between the Range</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s1 = 'Thrishank is a name'\n\ns2 = 'Kav'\n\nprint(len(s1))                           # 19\n\nprint(s1.upper())                        # THRISHANK IS A NAME\n\nprint(s1.lower())                        # thrishank is a name\n\nprint(s1.isupper())                      # False\n\nprint(s1.islower())                      # False\n\nprint(s1.startswith('Th'))               # True\n\nprint(s1.endswith('nk'))                 # False\n\nprint(s1.startswith('th'))               # False\n\nprint(s1.startswith(\" \", 1))             # False\n\nprint(s1.endswith('a', 5, len(s1)))      # False\n\nprint(s1.split(' '))                     # ['Thrishank', 'is', 'a', 'name']\n\nprint(s1.split('n'))                     # ['Thrisha', 'k is a ', 'ame']\n\nprint(s1.split('r', 1))                  # ['Th', 'ishank is a name']\n\nprint(''.join(s1))                       # Thrishank is a name\n\nprint(' '.join(s1))                      # T h r i s h a n k   i s   a   n a m e\n\nprint(s1.strip(\" \"))                     # Thrishank is a name\n\nprint(s1.lstrip(\" \"))                    # Thrishank is a name\n\nprint(s1.rstrip(\" \"))                    # Thrishank is a name\n\nprint(s1.replace('Thrishank', 'Kavya'))  # Kavya is a name\n\nprint(s1.replace('h', 'H'))              # THrisHank is a name\n\nprint(s1.find(s2))                       # -1\n\nprint(s1.find(s2, 0, 13))                # -1\n\nprint(s1.find('sha'))                    # 4</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Reverse a String</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 'Nani'<br><strong>Output:</strong> 'inaN'</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ns = input()\nrev = \"\"\n\nfor i in s:\n    rev = i + rev\n\nprint(rev)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># using Slicing\n\ns = input()\n\nprint(s[::-1])\n\n\n# s[x:y:z] gives substring from index x to y in steps of z</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check for Rotation</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s1 = \"ABCD\"</p>\n</div>\n<p>s2 = \"CDAB\"</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> Yes</p>\n</div>\n<p>Explaination :</p>\n<p>ABCD --&gt; BCDA --&gt; CDAB</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Solution\n\ndef areRotations(s1, s2):\n  if len(s1) != len(s2):\n    return False\n  temp = ''\n  temp = s1 + s1\n\n  return temp.find(s2) != -1\n\nprint(areRotations(\"ABCD\", \"CDAB\"))\n\nprint(areRotations(\"ABCD\", \"ABCA\"))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check for Palindrome</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 10-02-2001<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1002 20 01</p>\n</div>\n<p>----------------</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 'abba'<br><strong>Output:</strong> yes</p>\n</div>\n<p>----------------</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 'abA'<br><strong>Output:</strong> No</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ns = input()\nlow = 0\nhigh = len(s) - 1\n\nwhile low &lt; high:\n    if s[low] != s[high]:\n        print(\"No\")\n        break\n    low += 1\n    high -= 1\nelse:\n    print(\"Yes\")</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Using Slicing\n\ns = input()\n\nif s == s[::-1]:\n    print(\"Yes\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No\")</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check if a string is Subsequence</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s1 = 'ABCD'; s2 = 'AD'<br><strong>Output:</strong> True<br><strong>Input:</strong> s1 = \"ABCDE\"; s2 = \"AED\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> False</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef issubseq(s1, s2):\n  i, j = 0, 0\n\n  while i &lt; len(s1) and j &lt; len(s2):\n    if s1[i] == s2[j]:\n      j += 1\n    i += 1\n  return j == len(s2)\n\nprint(issubseq(\"ABCD\", \"AD\"))\nprint(issubseq(\"ABCDE\", \"AED\"))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Recursion\n\ndef issubseq(s1, s2, m, n):\n  if n == 0:\n    return True\n  if m == 0:\n    return False\n  if s1[m-1] == s2[n-1]:\n    return issubseq(s1, s2, m-1, n-1)\n  return issubseq(s1, s2, m-1, n)\n\nprint(issubseq(\"ABCD\", \"AD\", 4, 2))\nprint(issubseq(\"ABCDE\", \"AED\", 5, 3))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check for Anagram</h3>\n<p>Anagram : length &amp; character &amp; count should be same</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s1 = 'listen'</p>\n</div>\n<p> s2 = 'silent'</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> Yes</p>\n</div>\n<p>---------------------</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s1 = \"aabc\"</p>\n</div>\n<p> s2 = \"acab\"</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> Yes</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef anagram(s1, s2):\n  if len(s1) != len(s2):\n    return False\n  s1 = sorted(s1)\n  s2 = sorted(s2)\n\n  return s1 == s2\n\ns1 = \"listen\"\ns2 = \"silent\"\n\nprint(anagram(s1, s2))\n\ns1 = \"aabd\"\ns2 = \"acab\"\n\nprint(anagram(s1, s2))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef anagram(s1, s2):\n  if len(s1) != len(s2):\n    return False\n  count = [0] * 256\n\n  for i in range(len(s1)):\n    count[ord(s1[i])] += 1\n    count[ord(s2[i])] -= 1\n  for i in range(256):\n    if count[i] != 0:\n      return False\n  return True\n\ns1 = \"listen\"\ns2 = \"silent\"\n\nprint(anagram(s1, s2))\n\ns1 = \"aabd\"\ns2 = \"acab\"\n\nprint(anagram(s1, s2))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Leftmost Repeating Character</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> str = \"geeksforgeeks\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> 0<br><strong>Input:</strong> str = \"abbcc\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1<br><strong>Input:</strong> str = \"abcd\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> -1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Approach\n\ndef leftmost(str):\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    for j in range(i+1, len(str)):\n      if str[i] == str[j]:\n        return i\n  return -1\n\nstr = \"geeksforgeeks\"\n\nprint(leftmost(str))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Better Approach\n\nCHAR = 256\n\ndef leftmost(str):\n  count = [0] * CHAR\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    count[ord(str[i])] += 1\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    if count[ord(str[i])] &gt; 1:\n      return i\n\n  return -1\n\nstr = \"geeksforgeeks\"\n\nprint(leftmost(str))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1\n\nimport sys\n\nCHAR = 256\n\ndef leftmost(str):\n\n  fIndex = [-1] * CHAR\n  res = sys.maxsize\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n\n    if fIndex[ord(str[i])] == -1:\n\n      fIndex[ord(str[i])] = i\n\n    else:\n\n      res = min(res, fIndex[ord(str[i])])\n\n  return res\n\nstr = \"Thrishank\"\n\nprint(leftmost(str))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2\n\nCHAR = 256\n\ndef leftmost(str):\n  visited = [False] * CHAR\n  res = -1\n\n  for i in range(len(str) -1, -1, -1):\n    if visited[ord(str[i])] == True:\n      res = i\n    else:\n      visited[ord(str[i])] = True\n  return res\n\nstr = \"Thrishank\"\n\nprint(leftmost(str))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Leftmost Non-Repeating Character</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> str = 'geeksforgeeks'<br><strong>Output:</strong> 5<br><strong>Input:</strong> str = 'abcabc'<br><strong>Output:</strong> -1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef nonRep(str):\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    flag = False\n\n    for j in range(i+1, len(str)):\n      if str[i] == str[j]:\n        flag = True\n        break\n\n    if flag == False:\n      return i\n    return -1\n\nstr1 = \"aaa\"\n\nprint(nonRep(str1))\n\nstr1 = \"geeksforgeeks\"\n\nprint(nonRep(str1))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Better Solution\n\nCHAR = 256\n\ndef nonRep(str):\n  count = [0] * CHAR\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    count[ord(str[i])] += 1\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    if count[ord(str[i])] == 1:\n      return i\n  return -1\n\nstr1 = \"aaa\"\n\nprint(nonRep(str1))\n\nstr1 = \"geeksforgeeks\"\n\nprint(nonRep(str1))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1\n\nimport sys\n\nCHAR = 256\n\ndef nonRep(str):\n\n  fIndex = [-1] * CHAR\n  res = sys.maxsize\n\n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    if fIndex[ord(str[i])] == -1:\n      fIndex[ord(str[i])] = i\n    else:\n      fIndex[ord(str[i])] = -2\n\n  for i in range(CHAR):\n    if fIndex[i] &gt;= 0:\n      res = min(res, fIndex[i])\n\n  return res if res != sys.maxsize else -1\n\n\n\nstr1 = \"aaa\"\nprint(nonRep(str1))\n\nstr1 = \"geeksforgeeks\"\nprint(nonRep(str1))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Reverse Words in a String</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> str = \"Welcome to gfg\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> \"gfg to Welcome\"<br><strong>Input:</strong> str = 'abc'<br><strong>Output:</strong> abc</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\n'''\n1. Initialize an empty stack\n2. Split the string into words\n3. Push each word onto the stack\n4. Initialize the output string\n5. Pop words from the stack and append them to the output string\n6. Remove the trailing space and return the reversed string\n\n'''\n\ndef reverseWordsUsingStack(str):\n    stack = []\n    words = str.split()\n\n    for word in words:\n        stack.append(word)\n\n    reversed_str = \"\"\n\n    while stack:\n        reversed_str += stack.pop() + \" \"\n\n    return reversed_str.strip()\n\nstr = \"Welcome to gfg\"\nresult = reverseWordsUsingStack(str)\nprint(result)\n\n# Time Comeplexity : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Idea for O(1) Auxiliary Space Solution\n\n'''\n1. Reverse the individual word\n2. Reverse the whole string\n'''\n\ndef reverse(s, b, e):\n  while b &lt; e:\n    s[b], s[e] = s[e], s[b]\n    b += 1\n    e -= 1\n\ndef reversewords(s):\n  n = len(s)\n  b = 0\n  for e in range(n):\n    if s[e] == ' ':\n      reverse(s, b, e-1)\n      b = e + 1\n  reverse(s, b, n-1)\n  reverse(s, 0, n-1)\n\ns = list(\"Welcome to gfg\")\nreversewords(s)\nprint(\"\".join(s))</code></pre></figure></section>"}